From c3d02161ddfc12951eb4f1230d591097908563d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wang Lei <wangleiwave@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:46:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 059/116] UPSTREAM: x86: Bound Hygon non-temporal threshold [BZ
 #34875]

When a hypervisor exposes a Hygon CPUID vendor but omits cache topology,
shared_per_thread is zero.  The generic cache initialization detects the
invalid threshold and uses a 64 MiB fallback, but the Hygon-specific
adjustment then overwrites it with shared_per_thread * 3 / 8, restoring
zero.  memcpy and memmove consequently enter the non-temporal path for
small copies and can crash during process startup.

Only apply the Hygon heuristic when it produces a valid threshold.  This
preserves the generic fallback when cache information is unavailable while
retaining the Hygon tuning with valid cache data.

Fixes: 213ffdfbbae6 ("x86: Lower non-temporal copy threshold for Hygon")
Bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34875
Signed-off-by: Wang Lei <wangleiwave@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Adhemerval Zanella  <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>

(cherry picked from commit 16b35b8904e3f29ef504c34458716881e6abf280)
---
 NEWS                       |  2 ++
 sysdeps/x86/dl-cacheinfo.h | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index 1c561e43bf..63744fbeeb 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ The following bugs are resolved with this release:
     to 2.43
   [34734] libc: sparc: tcgetattr returns uninitialized bytes in c_cc[17]
     and c_cc[18]
+  [34875] string: 2.44 regression: Hygon non-temporal threshold can be
+    zero
 
 Version 2.44
 
diff --git a/sysdeps/x86/dl-cacheinfo.h b/sysdeps/x86/dl-cacheinfo.h
index 674545c796..2d6b979215 100644
--- a/sysdeps/x86/dl-cacheinfo.h
+++ b/sysdeps/x86/dl-cacheinfo.h
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /* Initialize x86 cache info.
    Copyright (C) 2020-2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
+   Copyright The GNU Toolchain Authors.
    This file is part of the GNU C Library.
 
    The GNU C Library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
@@ -1281,7 +1282,14 @@ dl_init_cacheinfo (struct cpu_features *cpu_features)
          Use 3/8 of the shared cache size per thread for memcpy and
          memmove.  The memset threshold has already been initialized
          above and is intentionally left unchanged.  */
-      non_temporal_threshold = shared_per_thread * 3 / 8;
+      unsigned long int hygon_non_temporal_threshold
+	  = shared_per_thread * 3 / 8;
+
+      /* Missing cache information makes shared_per_thread zero.  Do not
+	 replace the 64 MiB fallback with an invalid threshold.  */
+      if (hygon_non_temporal_threshold >= minimum_non_temporal_threshold
+	  && hygon_non_temporal_threshold <= maximum_non_temporal_threshold)
+	non_temporal_threshold = hygon_non_temporal_threshold;
     }
 
   tunable_size = TUNABLE_GET (x86_memset_non_temporal_threshold, long int, NULL);
-- 
